      "solution": "import sys\n\nn = int(input())\nbits = [int(input()) & 1 for _ in range(n)]\n\nchars = []\nfor i in range(0, len(bits), 8):\n    byte = 0\n    for b in bits[i:i+8]:\n        byte = (byte << 1) | b\n    chars.append(chr(byte))\n\nprint(\"\".join(chars))\n",
      "statement": "An undercover intelligence operative intercepted an image consisting of [[N]] grayscale pixels.\n\nA secret text message has been concealed inside the image using <<Least Significant Bit (LSB) steganography>>.\n\n### Rules\n1. Each [[pixel]] is an 8-bit integer between {{0}} and {{255}}.\n2. The least significant bit (LSB) of each pixel (`pixel % 2` or `pixel & 1`) stores one bit of the secret message.\n3. Every {{8}} consecutive bits form the 8-bit binary representation of an ASCII character, ordered from **most significant bit (MSB)** to **least significant bit (LSB)**.\n4. Extract all characters in order and print the resulting decoded message string.",
